<!DOCTYPE html>
<html metal:use-macro="context/@@pfas-macros/macros/page"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
      xmlns:tal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/tal"
      xmlns:metal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/metal">
<head>
  <title metal:fill-slot="title">Reference Weight Sets</title>
</head>
<body>
<tal:t metal:fill-slot="header-title">Reference Weight Sets</tal:t>
  <!-- the form's Save, pinned at the foot of the window -->
  <tal:ab metal:fill-slot="action-bar"><tal:sb tal:condition="view/can_configure" tal:define="sb_form string:weight-set-form; sb_label string:Save weight set"><div
      metal:use-macro="context/@@pfas-macros/macros/save-bar"></div></tal:sb></tal:ab>

<metal:content metal:fill-slot="content">
  <tal:def tal:define="purl view/portal_url; today view/today">

  <div class="pfas-why">
    A balance check is only as good as the weights it was performed with.
    These sets are calibrated by an <strong>external metrology laboratory</strong>
    &mdash; the point where the equipment chain leaves this laboratory, the same
    way a reagent's chain ends at its manufacturer's certificate. A set with no
    certificate or an expired calibration makes every
    balance check performed with it untraceable, and the Data Review
    traceability gate will reject the affected worksheets. All dates ISO 8601.
  </div>

  <p class="pfas-hint" tal:condition="not:view/can_configure">
    Weight sets and their metrology certificates are lab configuration: a
    Manager or LabManager records them.
  </p>

  <div class="pfas-card" tal:condition="view/can_configure">
    <h3>Add / update a weight set</h3>
    <p class="pfas-hint">Leave the identifier of an existing set unchanged to update it.</p>
    <form method="POST" id="weight-set-form" tal:attributes="action string:${purl}/@@pfas-weight-sets">
      <input type="hidden" name="action" value="save" />
      <input type="hidden" name="id" value="" tal:attributes="value request/form/id|nothing" />
      <div class="pfas-form-row">
        <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Set identifier</label>
          <input type="text" name="set_id" required placeholder="WS-001" /></div>
        <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Weight class</label>
          <input type="text" name="weight_class" placeholder="ASTM Class 1 / OIML E2" /></div>
        <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Serial number</label>
          <input type="text" name="serial_number" /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="pfas-form-field is-spaced"><label>Description</label>
          <input type="text" name="description" placeholder="1 mg - 100 g, 12 weights" /></div>

      <div class="pfas-check is-spaced">
        <label class="pfas-switch"><input type="checkbox" name="calibration_required" value="1" checked="checked" id="cal-req" /><span class="pfas-switch-track"></span></label>
        <label for="cal-req">Calibration required</label>
      </div>

      <div data-enable-if="calibration_required" data-enable-values="1">
      <h3 class="pfas-mt-md">External calibration</h3>
      <div class="pfas-form-row">
        <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Calibration service</label>
          <input type="text" name="cal_lab" required /></div>
        <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Its accreditation</label>
          <input type="text" name="cal_lab_accreditation"
                 placeholder="ISO/IEC 17025, scope no." /></div>
        <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Certificate number</label>
          <input type="text" name="cal_cert_number" required /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="pfas-form-row">
        <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Calibration date</label>
          <input type="date" name="cal_date" required /></div>
        <div class="pfas-form-field"><label>Calibration due</label>
          <input type="date" name="cal_due_date" required /></div>
      </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pfas-check">
        <label class="pfas-switch"><input type="checkbox" name="active" value="1" checked="checked" id="act" /><span class="pfas-switch-track"></span></label>
        <label for="act">In use</label>
      </div>
      <div class="pfas-form-field is-spaced"><label>Notes</label><input type="text" name="notes" /></div>
    </form>
  </div>

  <h3 class="pfas-card-title">Registered sets</h3>
  <table class="pfas-table log-table" data-col-resize="facility-weight-sets-log-table">
    <thead><tr>
      <th>Set</th><th>Class</th><th>Calibration service</th>
      <th>Certificate</th><th>Calibrated</th><th>Due</th><th>Status</th>
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tal:rows tal:repeat="ws view/weight_sets">
      <tr>
        <td><strong tal:content="ws/set_id">WS-001</strong>
            <span tal:condition="ws/description|nothing" class="pfas-muted-cell"
                  tal:content="string: — ${ws/description}"></span></td>
        <td tal:content="ws/weight_class|string:—">—</td>
        <td tal:content="ws/cal_lab|string:—">—</td>
        <td tal:content="ws/cal_cert_number|string:—">—</td>
        <td tal:content="ws/cal_date|string:—">—</td>
        <td tal:content="ws/cal_due_date|string:—">—</td>
        <td>
          <span tal:condition="not:ws/needs_calibration" class="badge badge-archived">NOT CALIBRATED</span>
          <span tal:condition="python:ws['needs_calibration'] and not ws['problems']" class="badge badge-ok">TRACEABLE</span>
          <tal:bad tal:condition="python:ws['needs_calibration'] and ws['problems']">
            <span class="badge badge-fail">NOT TRACEABLE</span>
            <span class="pfas-prob" tal:repeat="p ws/problems" tal:content="p"></span>
          </tal:bad>
        </td>
      </tr>
      </tal:rows>
      <tr tal:condition="not:view/weight_sets">
        <td colspan="7" class="pfas-muted-cell">
          No weight sets recorded. Until one is, every balance check traces
          to nothing.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  </tal:def>
</metal:content>
</body>
</html>
